  "evidence": "TEXT_C: Universal Basic Income with adult £89/week and pensioner £178/week; NHS +£6bn/year and free home social care for over‑65s; rent controls and end no‑fault evictions; cap pay ratios at 10:1; Land Value Tax replacing Council Tax/Business Rates; restorative justice and regulated drug policy (including cannabis legalisation); cancel Trident replacement and end arms export promotion; proportional representation, citizens’ assemblies; 10‑year Green New Deal with rapid renewable rollout and bans on fracking and most single‑use plastics. TEXT_E: Record NHS funding uplift, 50,000 more nurses, 40 hospitals; National Living Wage to two‑thirds of median earnings; implement Brexit, pursue global trade deals; maintain nuclear deterrent and exceed NATO 2%; 20,000 extra police, tougher sentences, more prison places; voter ID and retain First Past the Post; no rises in main income tax/NI/VAT, higher NI threshold, business rates cuts, SME R&D credit; Australian‑style points‑based immigration; Net Zero 2050 with 40GW offshore wind and plastics/producer‑responsibility measures; veterans’ protections and guarantees.",
  "reasoning": "The electorate weights Care and Equality most but also places substantial value on Loyalty and Authority; TEXT_E delivers strong Care (NHS, living wage) while clearly aligning with Loyalty and Authority (Brexit, defence, policing) and Proportionality (tax restraint, business focus). TEXT_C is very strong on Care and Equality but frequently runs counter to Loyalty and Authority (e.g., cancel Trident, restorative justice, PR) and leans into high‑salience sanctity/environmental purity that the profile weights least.",
